            "invalidation_reason": "4096 sits above 4080, where today's earlier long was stopped, and the 4084.40 H1 floor of the 06:52Z ledger, and below 4104 (09:00Z) and the 6 Nov high 4107.09; a trade there means the release reaction failed.",
            "invalidation_text": "any trade above 4096; the thesis is also broken by an M15 close above 4084.40 while EURUSD is back above 1.1199, a metals-only rebound of more than 0.9% with DXY flat, a Fed push-back on a December hike, or the US 2y giving back most of its CPI rise.",
            "main_alternative": {
              "market_move": "crowded-long dip buying returns, as on 6-9 Nov, and gold climbs back above 4096 before 13 Nov 08:00Z.",
              "probability_pct": 40.0
            },
            "mechanism": "the hot core print pushes the US front end toward a December hike (context: about a full hike priced, 2y +15-17 bp), raising real yields and firming the USD against a non-yielding asset whose speculators held 45% of open interest net long (3 Nov), with forced selling below the broken 8-9 Nov lows 4054.21/4054.83; captured 4139.17 (9 Nov close) to a 4050.952 bid at 15:05:02Z, -2.13% or -1.20 D1 ATR (ATR 73.38).",
            "missing_fields": [],
            "opposite_mechanism": "metals-specific dip buying by the crowded long base, as on 6-9 Nov, with mean reversion to the 20-day mean 4039.15 and support at the 6 Nov NFP low 4026.88, where last week's short stopped making progress (H1 low 4029.79).",
            "positioning": "speculators net long 179,548 of 399,169 (45%, COT 3 Nov, before the run to 4148.76; today's length not observed); flow-forcing levels are the broken 4054.2-4054.8 lows, then the 6 Nov D1 low 4026.88; ETF stocks were flat 2-6 Nov (GLD 1040.51 to 1041.37 t, IAU 461.62 to 460.81 t) and say nothing about 9-10 Nov dip demand. Crowd trade: long gold, wrong while gold stays under 4073.55-4084.40; this short is wrong on a metals-only rebound like 9 Nov 00:30-01:00Z (+0.91%, about 37 points, DXY -0.03%).",
            "priced": "prior_pricing AMBIGUOUS; the +2.74 ATR five-session run-up (3 Nov close 3938.16 to 9 Nov 4139.17) is fully given back; the capture sits +0.16 ATR over the 20-day mean 4039.15, -1.36 under the 50-day 4150.44 and -3.96 under the 200-day 4341.80; 20-day range 3870.03-4190.65; ATR percentile 15.3 before today; the dossier IN_LINE band (about -2.6% to +2.8%) contains today's move; the 48 h to 15 min drift, T0 level and implied move are not observed.",
